{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5","id":1270742,"title":"Wraith 5?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-25T19:18:25-08:00","id":1270742,"title":"Wraith 5?","content":"What would you want out of a hypothetical Wraith 5th Edition, circa 2024?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T07:02:33-08:00","id":1271763,"title":"","content":"The other/missing Guild books, a complete list of all Alt Arts that are missing from the 20th Ed. More example Artifacts, Far Shores sample realms, Spectral caste and Dark Arcanos Alt arts. <br /> <br /> Things like that, to start with. The missing Guild books would be really great, as I have wanted to see the Harbingers Guild book, I know that there is an online fan made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24734-deadman","name":"DeadMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T11:58:00-08:00","id":1272216,"title":"","content":"I think it would be nice if they made clear that the 6th Great Maelstrom did happen, preserving some of Ends of Empire while also showing how the Shadowlands has continued on <br /> <br /> I think it also might make sense to fold the Kuei-Jin and Mummy more clearly into Wraith/Risen cosmology and mechanics. That would be a way of preserving those game lines while also making things more updated, culturally sensitive, and cleaner mechanically","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T08:40:19-08:00","id":1279710,"title":"","content":"Trategos - I like your idea, but can Mummy really be folded in with Risen mechanics? The Undying are *not* undead. They're immortal and very much alive. Even the older ones, who had one foot in the grave were living beings (not that very many of those kinds remain, but there are some that do). With Kindred of the East, this makes more sense, as they're essentially an alternate version of Risen with vampiric qualities. Of course, mummies start as Wraiths and Wraith remnants, but given that whole alive again versus dead and walking thing, I'm not sure that they would fit so neatly. Then again, maybe with an explanation of mechanical differences, they could? I know that I'd like to see some love for Mummy: the Resurrection, however it can be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23923-lord-vil","name":"Lord Vil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23923_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T02:13:43-08:00","id":1280284,"title":"","content":"I don't really want a Wr5 if it's going to be like V5 (though Shadow Dice are obviously already part of the system, filling the niche Hunger fills in V5). Wr20 did enough to update the setting and rules, so that's perfect for me.<br /> <br /> However, a post-6GM setting update would be cool. Maybe as a V20.5 edition? In many ways, though, The Great War setting gives us a very good idea of what post-existence would be like during a Great Maelstrom. I always thought they put it out to give us a way to play those chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 01-12-2019, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T12:11:59-08:00","id":1280378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Vil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1279710#post1279710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trategos - I like your idea, but can Mummy really be folded in with Risen mechanics? The Undying are *not* undead. They're immortal and very much alive. Even the older ones, who had one foot in the grave were living beings (not that very many of those kinds remain, but there are some that do). With Kindred of the East, this makes more sense, as they're essentially an alternate version of Risen with vampiric qualities. Of course, mummies start as Wraiths and Wraith remnants, but given that whole alive again versus dead and walking thing, I'm not sure that they would fit so neatly. Then again, maybe with an explanation of mechanical differences, they could? I know that I'd like to see some love for Mummy: the Resurrection, however it can be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. The Kuei-Jin are only similar to the Risen on the surface level. Wraiths become Risen by choice, the Kuei-jin don't. The Risen by their nature are temporary, consumed with the life they had and finishing up unfinished business in the Skinlands. The Kuei-jin can exist for... well centuries or millennia. And they actively, through nearly all of the Dharmas, transcend their former humanity. And if a Risen is destroyed, they continue to exist as the wraith they were before becoming a Risen. A Kuei-jin is destroyed, they're destroyed.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that Risen can only come back in their corpse if it's intact while for a Kuei-jin, if the corpse was destroyed or cremated, the pieces/ashes will come back together to form their body upon rising. And it's also possible for Kuei-jin to rise in other people's corpses.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T22:39:04-08:00","id":1280446,"title":"","content":"Lord Vil and AkatsukiLeader13:<br /> <br /> My thinking behind this is to preserve the unique concepts of these two game lines while making them accessible to new and old players. I can honestly say that I love all the splats from the original WoD. I want to see them get their day with an updated veneer, and it make sense to address them in Wraith; not to go too meta, but maybe addressing Wraith, Mummy, and Kuei-Jin in one book might make it more appealing broadly to the masses...you know, like purifying the imperfections through merging the best part of the game lines..<br /> <br /> <br /> Seriously though, Wr5 had a section on Risen and Orpheus. W20 talks about the Changing Breeds. Maybe clarifying how Shadowlands denizens operate in one book is the way to go","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T20:37:52-08:00","id":1280602,"title":"","content":"Not to derail the conversation but here is a link to my solution about KotE and how I feel their anniversary edition should be handled.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/186083-i-think-kote-may-be-salvageable-for-a-20th-anniversary-run?p=193187#post193187\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/186083-i-think-kote-may-be-salvageable-for-a-20th-anniversary-run?p=193187#post193187\"> I think KotE may be salvageable for a 20th Anniversary run... - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/186083-i-think-kote-may-be-salvageable-for-a-20th-anniversary-run?p=193187#post193187\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/186083-i-think-kote-may-be-salvageable-for-a-20th-anniversary-run?p=193187#post193187 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The main thing they'd have to do is commit to any time &amp;quot;nostalgia-value&amp;quot; conflicts with &amp;quot;not being Orientalist douche-nozzles&amp;quot;, the latter needs to win. The Dharmas, disciplines, Hells, and mechanics around balance and extremes are interesting enough to give it a shot IMHO. Some </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T11:54:50-08:00","id":1280713,"title":"","content":"KotE, always felt like Risen with a little more Vampire in it, as they used some of the Wraith traits and then mixed in the East is better then the west stereotype that plagues the Old WoD lines, none of my players had any interest in playing it, Dark ages and Wild west Werewolf had a much stronger appeal.<br /> <br /> KotE could have been a great game, i think having one book that bridges the gaps between Wraith, KotE, and Mummy, would be great as the games have a lot in common, and trying to Kick start them individually would be costly, and Geist Sin-eaters uses much of the wraith ideas.<br /> <br /> as for Wr5th, we are still missing so much from the previous editions, that we should fill in those holes first and stay true to the game, wr20 or wr25 as is a lot closer to the truth of release, just came out. <br /> <br /> Post GM6 i think was left open to the storytellers, i would like to see Wraith opened up like they did for Vtm, Wta, and Mta<br /> so we could publish our own splat books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24734-deadman","name":"DeadMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T12:23:58-08:00","id":1280723,"title":"","content":"I mean, for me at least, a post-6GM game isn't that hard to conceive of;<br /> <br /> -Dialing back the destruction of the 6GM a little bit isn't too hard: just say that it wrecked Stygia and a bunch of Necropoli, just not so much that it left a smoking hole in the ground.<br /> -Having a Stygia game being about the slow recovery and rebuilding of the city. While all the remaining Hierarchy wraiths try to defend it from any opportunistic Heretics and Renegades.<br /> -Same with any Necropoli, in addition to deciding to try to re-establish contact with Stygia or choosing &quot;fuck it&quot; and doing their own thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T21:08:17-08:00","id":1280823,"title":"","content":"In terms of the metaplot I agree with tasti man LH. Make it a bit like Europe after the fall of the Western Roman empire.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, make things simpler and cleaner where possible. That goes for the underworld itself as well.<br /> <br /> In terms of presentation, group wraiths by Legions rather than Guilds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T09:52:43-08:00","id":1280922,"title":"","content":"Wraith has always been the odd game out in that it didn't do clean groupings. Because of that I'm not used to thinking of Wraiths in terms of Legions or Guilds, just Hierarch, Renegade, or Heretic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T11:35:27-08:00","id":1280948,"title":"","content":"Yeah Wraith when it comes to factions is kind of...odd.<br /> <br /> Going through Wr20, I get the impression that there's simultaneously so many factions, but nothing quite as mandatory as in the other gamelines. Like, being a Hierarch wraith, you need to pick between either being part of the military arm or the civilian arm. Guilds have a not-insubstantial amount of sub-factions within them. And because Heretics and Renegades aren't all united in a singular vision that you can have full freedom to make any Cult or Gang that you wish.<br /> <br /> Even with the splats, Wraith is almost a splat-less game. While yes, you're initially defined by Legion due to cause of death, there aren't any inherent mechanical effects from joining one. Even with the Guilds, while yes favoring one particular Arcanos will get you called by the Guild associated by it, but you aren't necessarily a Guildwraith just by having it.<br /> <br /> There's nothing as inherent as a Clan, a Tribe, or a Kith. You're just...your own wraith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T18:38:49-08:00","id":1281022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1280948#post1280948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> While yes, you're initially defined by Legion due to cause of death, there aren't any inherent mechanical effects from joining one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be something that changed. Maybe things associated with a cause of death are banes to wraiths, something that empowers a shadow for a while or could trigger a harrowing for a weakened or injured wraith. Maybe the legions offer tools for dealing with these situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T09:11:58-08:00","id":1281308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1281022#post1281022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That could be something that changed. Maybe things associated with a cause of death are banes to wraiths, something that empowers a shadow for a while or could trigger a harrowing for a weakened or injured wraith. Maybe the legions offer tools for dealing with these situations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hope not. Part of the backdrop of Wraith is that many kinds of death fall into more than one Legion and there is constant wrangling to divide up the recently deceased. The Legions are a political distinction, not a metaphysical one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T09:11:58-08:00","id":1281309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1281022#post1281022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That could be something that changed. Maybe things associated with a cause of death are banes to wraiths, something that empowers a shadow for a while or could trigger a harrowing for a weakened or injured wraith. Maybe the legions offer tools for dealing with these situations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hope not. Part of the backdrop of Wraith is that many kinds of death fall into more than one Legion and there is constant wrangling to divide up the recently deceased. The Legions are a political distinction, not a metaphysical one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T16:20:21-08:00","id":1281391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1280284#post1280284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, a post-6GM setting update would be cool. Maybe as a V20.5 edition? In many ways, though, The Great War setting gives us a very good idea of what post-existence would be like during a Great Maelstrom. I always thought they put it out to give us a way to play those chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>We used Great War for exactly that purpose instead of blowing up the setting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T05:06:50-08:00","id":1281488,"title":"","content":"Basically not to end up like VTM V5 ( just kidding, I dislike some aspects of it ),<br /> but in all seriousness, like others have stated, I'd wish to get a clear picture about the aftermath of the great maelstrom and the state of the good old shadowlands and for my personal wishlist, I hope they recognize dtf demons and maybe acknowledge the abyss ( maybe it's in the labyrinth, maybe not ), even a little cameo would work .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.com/v2/137x125q90/661/nSdTJk.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8612-magnus666","name":"magnus666","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T09:02:58-08:00","id":1281648,"title":"","content":"Much as I would love to see a Wraith 5th Edition, I'd never back it on Kickstarter. Its been four years for the 20th Edition. People make it all the way through college in less time then I've been waiting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3138-old-rusty-pipe","name":"Old Rusty Pipe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T10:01:18-08:00","id":1281654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Old Rusty Pipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1281648#post1281648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much as I would love to see a Wraith 5th Edition, I'd never back it on Kickstarter.</div> </div> </div> </div>...that's even assuming if it IS going to be on Kickstarter, considering Paradox and Mophidius aren't beholden to do the same things OPP does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T07:36:47-08:00","id":1282849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1281391#post1281391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We used Great War for exactly that purpose instead of blowing up the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. What in particular was useful from Wraith TGW for post- 6th great maelstrom setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T02:34:02-08:00","id":1283670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trategos_Sol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1282849#post1282849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. What in particular was useful from Wraith TGW for post- 6th great maelstrom setting?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That question is answered in the post quoted by the post you quoted. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T10:13:41-08:00","id":1284535,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm going to stick with 20th Anniversary Edition lines. If new editions after the time of 5th go back to using World of Darkness mechanics, not Chronicles of Darkness mechanics with some changes, and don't completely gut the concept and twist it into being all about hunting and the type of food that you drink fueling your powers (or similar nonsense in other 5th Edition venues), then I'll look at purchasing it. If others enjoy it, great. I'm not faulting other peoples' taste, but My personal interest is what they do in 20th Anniversary. I only want to see a 5th Edition (which would really be 4th for Wraith) to the extent of knowing that it would survive (pun intended) for future editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23923-lord-vil","name":"Lord Vil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23923_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T15:03:01-08:00","id":1286854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trategos_Sol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1282849#post1282849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. What in particular was useful from Wraith TGW for post- 6th great maelstrom setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like what Damien andadambeyoncelowe said, we used the maelstrom rules and other setting ideas introduced in Great War, just in a more contemporary way.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T04:58:11-08:00","id":1291090,"title":"","content":"My two cents.<br /> I think the main problem is that Wraith wasn't a very succesful game. We could debate about the reasons, but that fact still stands.<br /> So a Wraith 5 (it's 4th) should be different and put major changes into it. Some fixes and changes here and there on the current material wouldn't do. In the grand scheme they would feel like minor things I think. If I would be a publisher I'd say the premise is interesting but the execution didn't work well the first time around.<br /> Ultimately for Wraith 4 to be succesful it should become a different game from the one you love, otherwise it will stay in the afterlife (pun intended)<br /> <br /> But maybe I'm biased for the bad. I have both the 1st and 2nd edition corebooks in my bookshelf but never thought my groups could sink their teeth into them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T05:07:52-08:00","id":1291093,"title":"","content":"Firstly, I like Wraith 20. It's probably the best of all of them, and has enough material that you'd be hard pressed to ever run out of scenario ideas. <br /> <br /> But I don't think Wraith 5 is coming any time soon.V5 had a troubled launch last year, so while it may yet build momentum, there is no guarantee of any follow on games getting the 5th edition treatment just yet. Even then, Wraith is a way down the line and may just be too minor a commercial title to be a priority anyway. Moreover, the main emphasis of V5 was really highlighted in the Hunger Dice. While you can see a ready translation of this in Werewolf (Rage Dice) and even Mage (Paradox Dice), Wraith already has it's own way of handling inner strife and torment with it's Shadow rules. I'm not sure how it would translate, currently. <br /> <br /> In all, any new edition of Wraith has to be years away - and may not ever happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T20:16:48-07:00","id":1397885,"title":"","content":"Bumping this to note that, with the Wraith: Afterlife game on the horizon, it sounds like a Wraith5e is in the cards with Paradox's playbook.<br /> <br /> And additionally if we take into consideration that Orpheus trademark filed by Paradox a year ago...it sounds like the plan is to have Wraith and Orpheus exist side-by-side in the same edition, and not have the one &quot;ghost gameline&quot;. Which ideally means better integration among each other.<br /> <br /> (especially since, from what I've gathered, despite Wr20 having Or20 in the same book, there was not a resurgence of Wraith X Orpheus games occurring)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T09:09:55-07:00","id":1397990,"title":"","content":"Orpheus...? I'd rather have a focus on Wraith to be honest for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T09:42:57-07:00","id":1397998,"title":"","content":"Considering that 5e involves moving the metaplot forward past where they left off in 2004, the last we saw of the lands of the dead was shown in Orpheus. So I'd expect Wraith 5 to be a sequel to most of what Orpheus did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T09:56:03-07:00","id":1398001,"title":"","content":"I didn't - and don't - like the way Orpheus handled the Wraith settings. Basically, the former destroyed the latter. I will be disappointed if 5E Wraith is an utter reset of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T10:25:09-07:00","id":1398008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1397990#post1397990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orpheus...? I'd rather have a focus on Wraith to be honest for now.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1398001#post1398001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't - and don't - like the way Orpheus handled the Wraith settings. Basically, the former destroyed the latter. I will be disappointed if 5E Wraith is an utter reset of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would only swing things the other way if there was no Orpheus at all, since that has garnered its own fanbase. Would cause a stir if it wasn't around.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, if the direction of the rest of WoD5e is anything to go by, it's mostly going to progress through the WoN events so that they happened, just not to the point that everything is unplayable. So...no, I don't think we're going as far as &quot;Underworld is a smoking hole in the ground&quot; in a post-6GM world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T10:54:22-07:00","id":1398017,"title":"","content":"This. My own preference would be that a new, post-Hierarchy society has emerged in the wake of the last Great Maelstrom, and that the new status quo involves wraiths living on both sides of the Shroud: the ones living in the Shadowlands represent something more akin to classic wraiths, while the ones living in the Skinlands are more like the Spirits featured in Orpheus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T11:29:36-07:00","id":1398026,"title":"","content":"Just...as long as they don't go so far the other way that we get into &quot;the Second Inquisition has absorbed Orpheus into its organization and has become their official ghost-hunting arm&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T11:44:36-07:00","id":1398030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1398026#post1398026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just...as long as they don't go so far the other way that we get into &amp;quot;the Second Inquisition has absorbed Orpheus into its organization and has become their official ghost-hunting arm&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that sounds like a nightmare, lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T11:46:34-07:00","id":1398031,"title":"","content":"Yeah; I have concerned about that sort of thing, too. On the one hand, bringing in Orpheus-like elements greatly increases the interaction between the living and the dead; so it wouldn't surprise me if the Second Inquisition had a branch wielding Orpheus-tech to hunt ghosts. But it wouldn't be Orpheus (which was destroyed) or its successor; that company's mission statement is pretty much the opposite of the Second Inquisition mindset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T17:04:53-07:00","id":1398260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1398001#post1398001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't - and don't - like the way Orpheus handled the Wraith settings. Basically, the former destroyed the latter. I will be disappointed if 5E Wraith is an utter reset of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Orpheus didn't kill Wraith. Wraith was killed several years before Orpheus came out in Ends of Empire, which was part of the Revised Edition start as well what caused the new Revised Era lines of Hunter, Demon and Mummy but not Orpheus. While the metaplot events were started by those events, Orpheus and the titular Orpheus Group pre-exist the end of WtO.<br /> <br /> In fact, you could completely remove the Sixth Great Maelstrom (and for that matter the other Great Calamities of 1999) and Orpheus would still exist in-universe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1398031#post1398031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah; I have concerned about that sort of thing, too. On the one hand, bringing in Orpheus-like elements greatly increases the interaction between the living and the dead; so it wouldn't surprise me if the Second Inquisition had a branch wielding Orpheus-tech to hunt ghosts. But it wouldn't be Orpheus (which was destroyed) or its successor; that company's mission statement is pretty much the opposite of the Second Inquisition mindset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. People forget but the Orpheus Group and it's successor, Lazarus Redux, were not the only Projectors in town. There was both NextWorld and Terrel and Squib, the former being a private security firm that had dark side, carrying out things like assassinations, espionage and blackmail. And while the metaplot is vague as to what ultimately happens to NextWorld, like Orpheus and T&amp;S it ceases to exist. Perhaps it was folded into a covert agency like the Second Inquisition.<br /> <br /> But the thing is, it doesn't have to be NextWorld because there already is a government agency that has it's fingers in projecting, the NSA. In the backstory, the NSA was involved in the early days of the OG and Project Flatline, their first big projecting experiment that ended in disaster. And once Orpheus gets attacked, steps in to finish off the company, take/destroy it's records and clean up any loose ends, using Death Merchants (mercs and assassins that can project) to hunt down Orpheus survivors and other dirty deeds. Eventually they created their own projector outfit, Operation: Black Mercury.<br /> <br /> Given the origins and nature of the Second Inquisition, having Black Mercury around and coming into contact with the founders of SI wouldn't be a stretch. Though personally, I'd keep SI and OBM separate as having the SI with access to projectors would make them a much worse threat for most non-Hecata vampires. Both groups have their own areas of operation so let them handle their own things and only work together with their sphere meet. OBM agents encounter some serious vampire activity? Send word to the SI so they can deal with it. SI agents come into contact with ghost activity? Call OBM to handle it. Hecata trafficking in Pigment? Well then that's the time for the SI and OBM to get together to deal with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T20:11:17-07:00","id":1398280,"title":"","content":"Since when was Orpheus pre-6M? It has a WHOLE bunch of elementals that clash with WTO from what little I remember when I heard somethings about it. Especially with Spectres apparently able to make &quot;hives&quot; beyond the shroud somehow (without Embody or even having any Fetters- Spectres can't remain outside the Tempest or the Underworld for long with a Fetter or they die), weird things with Oblivion somehow being personified as &quot;Grand Mother&quot;, and in general Stygia or the Jade Kingdom (the major Dark Kingdoms before 6M) weren't even mentioned at all whatsoever. I've always seen Orpheus as something that was post-6M or in its own hazy continuum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 06-23-2020, 02:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T10:33:05-07:00","id":1398380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1398280#post1398280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since when was Orpheus pre-6M? It has a WHOLE bunch of elementals that clash with WTO from what little I remember when I heard somethings about it. Especially with Spectres apparently able to make &quot;hives&quot; beyond the shroud somehow (without Embody or even having any Fetters- Spectres can't remain outside the Tempest or the Underworld for long with a Fetter or they die), weird things with Oblivion somehow being personified as &quot;Grand Mother&quot;, and in general Stygia or the Jade Kingdom (the major Dark Kingdoms before 6M) weren't even mentioned at all whatsoever. I've always seen Orpheus as something that was post-6M or in its own hazy continuum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Game mechanics aside, that stuff is the metaplot of Orpheus which as I said, does require the metaplot of WtO. But the Orpheus Group and the events that led to it's creation happened well before the 6GM. It's why the Orpheus appendix can exist in Wr20, because the Orpheus Group and projectors in general didn't require the 6GM unlike with HtR, DtF and MtR. And if the 6GM didn't happen, the Orpheus Group, their competitors and the Flatliners would still exist because all that stuff was happening in the mid-90s, several years before the 6GM happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T10:52:10-07:00","id":1398385,"title":"","content":"Retroactively. That is, there was nothing said in any book anywhere about the Orpheus Group prior to the publication of <b>Orpheus</b> in 2003; but yes, there were events described in <b>Orpheus</b>' backstory that predated the Maelstrom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T11:54:09-07:00","id":1398394,"title":"","content":"Oh, and a slightly more depressing note, with the existence of Afterlife and Paradox's track-record when it comes to WoD5e...<br /> <br /> ...I think we can also take this as solid confirmation that there aren't going to be anymore official Wr20 books coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T17:28:09-07:00","id":1398469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1398394#post1398394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and a slightly more depressing note, with the existence of Afterlife and Paradox's track-record when it comes to WoD5e...<br /> <br /> ...I think we can also take this as solid confirmation that there aren't going to be anymore official Wr20 books coming.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really, really recommend Necropolis Venezia ( English Edition) on the Vault, its awsome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T17:36:02-07:00","id":1400427,"title":"","content":"I would love a wraith 5e - but it absolutely cannot be done by the same leadership that was delegated to do so. Delays aside, the worst aspect was the &quot;nerfing&quot; for the sake making it lowest on the totem pole when compared to other lines (literally, the explanation given by the chief editor or whatever was that someone has to be the weakest and it was a conscious decision to make wraiths do) gutted the game in terms of immersion.<br /> <br /> Pretty much every guild (and by extension Wraith) isnt really scary from a system perspective. You have to dispense with the system to actual match the lore and immersion required of awe inspiring powers (not any more!). In some cases, some arts became worse than the mundane equivalent of picking up a sword, a pen, or hammer... Literal traps.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4487-nerhesi","name":"Nerhesi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T02:17:08-07:00","id":1400477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nerhesi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Delays aside, the worst aspect was the &quot;nerfing&quot; for the sake making it lowest on the totem pole when compared to other lines (literally, the explanation given by the chief editor or whatever was that someone has to be the weakest and it was a conscious decision to make wraiths do) gutted the game in terms of immersion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep that's why I only use Arcanoi from 2nd Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T08:15:42-07:00","id":1400523,"title":"","content":"Are we talking about Wr20 now? Or did Paradox assign someone to do some initial development work on Wr5 that I haven't heard about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T21:33:48-07:00","id":1400627,"title":"","content":"I played Wraith using the rules from V5. Translation is actually pretty seamless and it worked really well. Highly recommended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Mercy of Order is Justice&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1391-aeoris","name":"Aeoris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T03:15:00-07:00","id":1400676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeoris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1400627#post1400627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I played Wraith using the rules from V5. Translation is actually pretty seamless and it worked really well. Highly recommended.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Um, how? V5 doesn't use pools so what did you do for Pathos/Angst etc. And based on our games of V5 how were you not falling into a Harrowing every ten rolls or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T19:31:57-07:00","id":1400882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1400676#post1400676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Um, how? V5 doesn't use pools so what did you do for Pathos/Angst etc. And based on our games of V5 how were you not falling into a Harrowing every ten rolls or so.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you mean V5 doesn\u2019t use pools?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T07:13:11-07:00","id":1401684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nerhesi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1400427#post1400427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would love a wraith 5e - but it absolutely cannot be done by the same leadership that was delegated to do so. Delays aside, the worst aspect was the &quot;nerfing&quot; for the sake making it lowest on the totem pole when compared to other lines (literally, the explanation given by the chief editor or whatever was that someone has to be the weakest and it was a conscious decision to make wraiths do) gutted the game in terms of immersion.<br /> <br /> Pretty much every guild (and by extension Wraith) isnt really scary from a system perspective. You have to dispense with the system to actual match the lore and immersion required of awe inspiring powers (not any more!). In some cases, some arts became worse than the mundane equivalent of picking up a sword, a pen, or hammer... Literal traps.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well if they were nerfed in wr20, in wr5 they will be weaker than regular humans... I mean look to what they did to vampires in v5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24832,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","user":"blailton","date":". 07-08-2020, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T15:38:55-07:00","id":1401789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1401684#post1401684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well if they were nerfed in wr20, in wr5 they will be weaker than regular humans... I mean look to what they did to vampires in v5</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing they did to vampires in V5 is have them play more like vampires. Moreover, Wraith is not the type of game where you spend much time worrying about the respective power levels of the characters. It is, of the original classic lines, the purest attempt at making a game about personal horror and the big design questions should be in whether it can deliver that experience rather than whether powers have been \u2018nerfed\u2019 or not. It is not a supers game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T16:55:52-07:00","id":1401808,"title":"","content":"Wraith has more themes than the whole personal horror spiel- it had intrigue, empire-building, an eternal war against Oblivion, and a general dystopic feel to it. The only real circumstance of personal horror is the Shadow and the fact that your dead, but like I said before it has ALOT more personality than that. Besides the Arcanoi of 2nd edition were completely fine the way they were and was moderate. Their disruption in Wr20 was unneeded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T17:31:10-07:00","id":1401811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1401808#post1401808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wraith has more themes than the whole personal horror spiel- it had intrigue, empire-building, an eternal war against Oblivion, and a general dystopic feel to it. The only real circumstance of personal horror is the Shadow and the fact that your dead, but like I said before it has ALOT more personality than that. Besides the Arcanoi of 2nd edition were completely fine the way they were and was moderate. Their disruption in Wr20 was unneeded.</div> </div> </div> </div>The various powers you can or can\u2019t get in a game, or whether they have been nerfed or not, is not a theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T02:31:20-07:00","id":1401876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1401789#post1401789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only thing they did to vampires in V5 is have them play more like vampires. Moreover, Wraith is not the type of game where you spend much time worrying about the respective power levels of the characters. It is, of the original classic lines, the purest attempt at making a game about personal horror and the big design questions should be in whether it can deliver that experience rather than whether powers have been \u2018nerfed\u2019 or not. It is not a supers game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires are weaker in v5 than they are in VtM. Ex: Celerity.<br /> <br /> Not every Wr. Chronicle is personal horror.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1187957-what-is-with-the-significant-nerf-to-arcanoi-in-wraith-20?p=1320010#post1320010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wraith is at it\u2019s core a game about emotions, regret, unfinished business and hanging on to your existence in a hostile environment where the greatest enemy you will ever face is yourself. <br /> <br /> It is about learning to let go and about how hard that is.<br /> <br /> But it also is about history, you can meet Wraiths from radically different times sitting at the same table.<br /> <br /> But like pointed out it is also about a very real war for existence itself, not only for you but for everyone. Oblivion would just as gladly devour the Skinlands as it would the Shadowlands. If the Wraiths fail to keep Spectres and Oblivion at bay it may mean an end to everything. This war is just as important as any war fough by the Garou.<br /> <br /> Wraith is about lot of things. One chronicle may be all about seeking personal Transcendence while another may be about hanging on to your Fetters and trying to guide your living relatives on the right path. While another may be about some crazed sonsofbitches going on a Helldive to prevent the next big Onceborn plot while making sure that nothing awakes the Neverborn. Another game could be about exploring the far reaches or fighting the Vampires of the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra.<br /> <br /> What I am saying is that the structure of the game should help us tell all of these stories.<br /> <br /> Sometimes it is really smallscale and personal and sometimes it is about Death Gods.<br /> <br /> Personally Wraith has always been my favourite WoD gameline, even though due to popular demand Vampire has been the most played, and as such owning almost every book for the line the changes aren\u2019t a big deal for me. I can always use the modern Wr20 rules while keeping the power level as it was. And like said there are many ways to approach Wraith and in a lot of them power level does not really matter. That said I have always been of the opinion that a games rule set must allow for players to achieve same levels of power as NPC\u2019s of their type. Even if the chance of that happening is miniscule. That is why I like having Disciplines up to level 9 available in VtM, Archspheres in Mage the possibility to transcend in to a powerful spirit in WtA Etc. Now with C20 we finally have rules for Siochain and the Arts have been boosted to Fae like power. But sadly Wr20 does not give us any tools on how to become a Death Lord or any chance to rival Charon, the only way the rules even imply becoming something more, or less depending on how you see it but definately more powerful, is through becoming a Spectre and rising to Onceborn status but even that is mostly in ST hands, and then there are the Ferrymen but even though they gain much in their transformation they too use the same Arcanoi and that means that those Arcanoi must be enough to portray what they can do.<br /> <br /> So in summary while I do agree that in, perhaps, the most Wraith games powerlevel does not matter as they are much more about emotions and personal tribulations than about what powers you have still not having those powers that can help portray the other stories around anymore does indeed shut down story possibilities. And that is always bad no matter how one looks at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T02:44:52-07:00","id":1401879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1401876#post1401876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are weaker in v5 than they are in VtM. Ex: Celerity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does that have anything to do with Wraith? And to answer that particular point, Celerity works with much more elegance in V5 than it ever did in previous editions, largely because it brought it back to narrative themes rather than just being a power stat that, somewhat ironically, tended to reduce combat rounds to a crawl as players performed multiple actions. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not every Wr. Chronicle is personal horror. </div> </div> </div>Maybe not, but Shadowplay is at the core of the game and the fundamental themes running through the game as a whole has everything to do with personal horror.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Wraith is at it\u2019s core a game about emotions, regret, unfinished business and hanging on to your existence in a hostile environment where the greatest enemy you will ever face is yourself.</i> </div> </div> </div>Sounds a lot like personal horror to me....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 07-09-2020, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T04:17:30-07:00","id":1401889,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2517_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2517\" data-vbnamecard=\"2517\">Trippy</a> agreed. The point of playing WoD (and I guess CoD) is to experience the horror and romance of playing a supernatural creature, in this case a ghost. It\u2019s not to see how many cool powers you can get. I mean, you can play that way, but I don\u2019t, and neither does any other group I\u2019ve ever played with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T05:35:05-07:00","id":1401901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1401879#post1401879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does that have anything to do with Wraith? .</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires became more weak in v5, so I think Wr will became even more weak in Wr5. Thats all. There's nothing to do with more or less elegance, personal horror or etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T05:37:16-07:00","id":1401902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it\u2019s not to see how many cool powers you can get. </div> </div> </div>Who said that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T05:55:05-07:00","id":1401908,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24832_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24832\" data-vbnamecard=\"24832\">blailton</a> I did. I was exaggerating to make a point. Sorry. I just woke up when I posted that and I was suffering from Social Media Withdrawal Syndrome \ud83d\ude0a.<br /> <br /> Also, I do like intrigue and politics in my WoD games and I even enjoy occasional doses of combat (it adds flavor, like sprinkles on a cupcake). When I say \u201cpersonal horror\u201d I mean \u201cangst.\u201d I think you guys might mean something different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T12:38:36-07:00","id":1401945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1401901#post1401901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires became more weak in v5, so I think Wr will became even more weak in Wr5. Thats all. There's nothing to do with more or less elegance, personal horror or etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I flatly refute that. It is a dumb way of comparing games, it is not true, and the comments have nothing to do with the possibilities of Wraith5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T14:07:11-07:00","id":1401962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1401889#post1401889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2517_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2517\" data-vbnamecard=\"2517\">Trippy</a> agreed. The point of playing WoD (and I guess CoD) is to experience the horror and romance of playing a supernatural creature, in this case a ghost. It\u2019s not to see how many cool powers you can get. I mean, you can play that way, but I don\u2019t, and neither does any other group I\u2019ve ever played with.</div> </div> </div> </div>WoD is a freeform tabletop. It most certainly isn't all about romance (lmao) and horror is a given fiat anyways. Also the topic is about Arcanoi nerfs, not accumulating as much as a PC can get.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well, I flatly refute that. It is a dumb way of comparing games, it is not true, and the comments have nothing to do with the possibilities of Wraith5.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">How is seeing the outcome from one edition not liable to be a metric to weigh when its going to come to the other editions? I'm holding out to see what will they do with Werewolf and if my fears are confirmed, I'll just extrapolate to how Wraith 5 is going to turn out.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T14:40:24-07:00","id":1401971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1401962#post1401962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> WoD is a freeform tabletop. It most certainly isn't all about romance (lmao) and horror is a given fiat anyways. Also the topic is about Arcanoi nerfs, not accumulating as much as a PC can get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the topic is not about 'Arcanoi nerfs'. Last time I checked, it was about a possible Wraith 5.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How is seeing the outcome from one edition not liable to be a metric to weigh when its going to come to the other editions? I'm holding out to see what will they do with Werewolf and if my fears are confirmed, I'll just extrapolate to how Wraith 5 is going to turn out. </div> </div> </div></span></span></span>Because it is dumb metric. The moment that storytelling games are more about comparing powers than story, is the point where the entire concept is lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T03:17:01-07:00","id":1402032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1401901#post1401901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires became more weak in v5, so I think Wr will became even more weak in Wr5. Thats all. There's nothing to do with more or less elegance, personal horror or etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they nerfed Disciplines in V5 for it's own sake. <br /> <br /> They did 3 main things with the disciplines:<br /> <br /> 1. They consolidated disciplines, especially ultra-exclusive disciplines like Serpentis and Obtenebration, and made it so that they share a discipline with at least another clan.<br /> <br /> 2. They gave each discipline a number of points at which the player would have to choose between two different powers.<br /> <br /> 3. No more &quot;Stat boost&quot; disciplines. <br /> <br /> I think the reason for the first is that it means players aren't always reaching for that obscure clan with it's special powers, or if a player wants a certain power, he has a couple of options of how you might gain that discipline.<br /> <br /> The second and third help to ensure that two vampires with the same disciplines (and the same clan) are not always going to be the same, and all have special things they can do.<br /> <br /> If I had a complaint it would be that some of the options presented are sub par compared to their counterparts, but this can be fixed.<br /> <br /> As far as Wraith, none of these 3 concerns apply to Arcanoi. Wraiths take whatever arcanos they like from the start, and are pre-built for having multiple arts at every level. Arcanoi are untethered to any splat, so Wraith players have maximal freedom when choosing them.<br /> <br /> I think as far as Arcanoi are concerned, the main issue is clarity. How does this Art affect the world of the living? the dead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T20:44:26-07:00","id":1402353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1402032#post1402032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think as far as Arcanoi are concerned, the main issue is clarity. How does this Art affect the world of the living? the dead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually it's pretty explicit which Arcanos does/does not do anything in the Skinlands. Arcanoi like Embody, Outrage, and Pandemonium are obvious (and whose Difficulty is based on the Shroud rating). Other times it's kind of inconsequential on if it does/doesn't do anything in the Skinlands (Moliate) or completely not relevant to it (Argos).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T11:39:25-07:00","id":1402439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1402353#post1402353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Usually it's pretty explicit which Arcanos does/does not do anything in the Skinlands. Arcanoi like Embody, Outrage, and Pandemonium are obvious (and whose Difficulty is based on the Shroud rating). Other times it's kind of inconsequential on if it does/doesn't do anything in the Skinlands (Moliate) or completely not relevant to it (Argos).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Check the &quot;systems&quot; text at the front of every Arcanoi for that information. I think the text on that is clear, however I don't think it's simple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2317,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","user":"Callishka","date":".  typo 07-12-2020, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T19:44:23-07:00","id":1403467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nerhesi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1400427#post1400427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would love a wraith 5e - but it absolutely cannot be done by the same leadership that was delegated to do so. Delays aside, the worst aspect was the &quot;nerfing&quot; for the sake making it lowest on the totem pole when compared to other lines (literally, the explanation given by the chief editor or whatever was that someone has to be the weakest and it was a conscious decision to make wraiths do) gutted the game in terms of immersion.<br /> <br /> Pretty much every guild (and by extension Wraith) isnt really scary from a system perspective. You have to dispense with the system to actual match the lore and immersion required of awe inspiring powers (not any more!). In some cases, some arts became worse than the mundane equivalent of picking up a sword, a pen, or hammer... Literal traps.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1400477#post1400477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep that's why I only use Arcanoi from 2nd Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> -Moliate Common 2: Sculpt lets you get Claws and Fangs\u2026which specifically grant you the ability to deal Aggravated. And this is a Common Art, and only at rating 2, meaning any non-Masquer wraith could learn it. <br /> <br /> -Usury Common 3: Corpus Conduit lets the users steal health. While it is just bashing damage if you use it on an undamaged target, it still adds up over time. And that yes, you get more mileage if the target is already damaged. However, the Difficulty is always determined by max health level. Which on non-wraith targets, is usually always 7 at the highest. So\u2026in crossover games, Usurers do have a pretty good advantage against the other splats. <br /> <br /> -Inhabit Initiate 3: Smith's Tenacity allows the wraith to soak Aggravated damage. Which yes, the caveat is that in order to learn it is that you need to be in the Artificer Guild to learn it, but technically that Guildwraith could still teach it to anyone else (which even then, that's up to the ST on how strict/loose the Guilds are at teaching non-Guildswraiths Initiate Arts).<br /> <br /> -Keening Common 4: Crescendo, which is the closest thing to an AoE attack in Wraith. A little bit of a &quot;but\u2026&quot; since it targets everyone in hearing range, including your allies, but still pretty powerful. This is compounded with a new rule when it comes to Keening where using it across the Shroud incurs a -4 to the Difficulty\u2026meaning if you're targetting someone across the Shroud you're always going to be rolling at Difficult 4-6. Which is a pretty good equalizer to it's &quot;two successes count as 1 level of damage&quot;. And then there's it's Initiate version Banshee, which swaps it out with aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Since I know this is about Outrage Common 5 - Obliviate: no, I don't think it's a matter of the Big Damage power getting nerfed, it's more about &quot;expanding the other powers so Obliviate isn't the One True Answer to Big Damage&quot;. And even ignoring that\u2026it's Angst penalty only went up by 1. 3 Angst isn't that big of a leap from 2 Angst. And someone in your Circle should know Castigate to lower Angst anyways because\u2026why wouldn't you?<br /> <br /> If the concern is Pathos cost\u2026well:<br /> <br /> 1.) Your character should be regularly engaging in their Passions because they should be Things-they-were-going-to-do-anyways and how that's kind of the whole point of the game. Your character has no excuse for not going into an encounter will full Pathos, nor neglecting their Passions.<br /> <br /> 2.) Even if that isn't the case, your characters should also be stocking up on Soulfire Crystals to pop and gain Pathos back. They have no excuse at not being friends with the local Usurer, or having one in their Circle.<br /> <br /> And that's without getting into how INSANELY DURABLE wraiths are:<br /> <br /> -Every single wraith starts off with 10 base health, something the other splats can only achieve with either Merits or certain powers.<br /> <br /> -Insubstantiality trivializing Skinlands damage to only the 1 bashing damage.<br /> <br /> -They're the only splat that doesn't insta-die from aggravated damage overflow. And that they have a chance on coming back from, an option none of the other splats really have.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T20:09:28-07:00","id":1403474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1403467#post1403467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is compounded with a new rule when it comes to Keening where using it across the Shroud incurs a -4 to the Difficulty\u2026meaning if you're targetting someone across the Shroud you're always going to be rolling at Difficult 4-6.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, unless I'm reading you wrong, I believe using Keening across the Shroud is harder, not easier, than not doing so.<br /> <br /> The line is: &quot;Keening powers can be applied across the Shroud at an <b>additional </b>difficulty of the current Shroud rating \u20134&quot; (Wr20 p. 182) ... emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> That is not clearly written, but it seems to be saying that the Difficulty goes UP from its base by [Shroud Rating - 4]. So If the Difficulty for the Art is 6, and the local Shroud is, say, Rating 7, then that's [7 - 4] = 3. Diffculty 6 + Difficulty 3 is Difficulty 9 total.<br /> <br /> Or I'm reading the rules totally wrong. In any case, it's kind of a mess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T21:01:38-07:00","id":1403480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Callishka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1403474#post1403474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately, unless I'm reading you wrong, I believe using Keening across the Shroud is harder, not easier, than not doing so.<br /> <br /> The line is: &quot;Keening powers can be applied across the Shroud at an <b>additional </b>difficulty of the current Shroud rating \u20134&quot; (Wr20 p. 182) ... emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> That is not clearly written, but it seems to be saying that the Difficulty goes UP from its base by [Shroud Rating - 4]. So If the Difficulty for the Art is 6, and the local Shroud is, say, Rating 7, then that's [7 - 4] = 3. Diffculty 6 + Difficulty 3 is Difficulty 9 total.<br /> <br /> Or I'm reading the rules totally wrong. In any case, it's kind of a mess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we had discussed this elsewhere... :P<br /> <br /> Which is why I go with my interpretation, because your interpretation suggests an additional calculation to Difficulty that none of the other Arcanoi uses, and that overcomplicates that calculation in the process.<br /> <br /> A flat -4 bonus to Difficulty makes a ton more sense then adding [Shroud rating - 4], on top of the math making the Difficulty go over 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T23:59:11-07:00","id":1403492,"title":"","content":"It did seem familiar, this Keening situation :^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T16:19:34-07:00","id":1439919,"title":"","content":"A restoration of the impressive nature of level 4 and 5 arcanoi to the 2E levels, but with added clarity to rules where needed. Basically undoing the decision that was taken to make wraiths the weakest of supers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4487-nerhesi","name":"Nerhesi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T16:23:16-07:00","id":1439920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nerhesi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1439919#post1439919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A restoration of the impressive nature of level 4 and 5 arcanoi to the 2E levels, but with added clarity to rules where needed. Basically undoing the decision that was taken to make wraiths the weakest of supers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno about that, the level 4-5 powers aren't really pushovers either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T16:28:24-07:00","id":1439924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1403467#post1403467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> No.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can disagree all you want, but the line developer literally indicated otherwise in an interview. It was a conscious decision to nerf the power of arcanoi and make wraiths the weakest of the supers. I can't argue logically argue with his decision because it is a subjective decision so he is welcome to it, and his execution of it.<br /> <br /> Your argument however, is logically not sound. Not only is it contrary to the opinion and implementation by the Wraith 20th ed developer, your counter arguments are based on a false premise:<br /> If there exists useful powers, it does not mean, that other powers are utterly crap for their level or are complete traps (including two of the ones you indicate above).<br /> <br /> Now, given the literal admission of how wraith arcanoi were nerfed, and the problems that several people have with it - It is a safe bet that the return of powerful arcanoi (that are not trap choices) is something that many people would want (because they have already said so in this thread and others).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4487-nerhesi","name":"Nerhesi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T16:30:23-07:00","id":1439926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nerhesi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1439924#post1439924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can disagree all you want, but the line developer literally indicated otherwise in an interview.</div> </div> </div> </div>...except that doesn't matter if you actually sit down to look at the text, not just choosing to ignore it just because a dev said something to override it.<br /> <br /> And I'm running a Wraith game right now and know that Wr20 rules hold up for the most part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T16:38:44-07:00","id":1439930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1439926#post1439926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...except that doesn't matter if you actually sit down to look at the text, not just choosing to ignore it just because a dev said something to override it.<br /> <br /> And I'm running a Wraith game right now and know that Wr20 rules hold up for the most part.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As per the other post. Literally the text disagrees with - level 4 and 5 powers, in many cases, were made significantly worse than their 2e counterparts. You even reference them in your example above and say &quot;it's not a big deal&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's not a big deal is subjective - but you've already conceded they've become worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4487-nerhesi","name":"Nerhesi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T16:44:09-07:00","id":1439933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nerhesi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1439930#post1439930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a big deal is subjective - but you've already conceded they've become worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>No I didn't.<br /> <br /> I said that any differences weren't enough of a big deal, and as such not bad enough to warrant the &quot;these powers are WAY worse then past editions' powers&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T16:47:30-07:00","id":1439937,"title":"","content":"Also at this point <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4487-nerhesi\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4487\" data-vbnamecard=\"4487\">Nerhesi</a> I'm not going to bother responding to you again on this line of thinking in this thread. Taking it to the other thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T09:55:40-07:00","id":1440057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nerhesi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a safe bet that the return of powerful arcanoi (that are not trap choices) is something that many people would want (because they have already said so in this thread and others).</div> </div> </div> </div>With the way of how V5 was done, I'm not hopeful on how Wraith &quot;5&quot; will come about. Wraith barely even has a fanbase, so even with alot people going to disagree with any potential changes, I doubt any care would be considered. I'm just waiting to see how they're going to do Werewolf &quot;5&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 03-15-2021, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T22:01:03-07:00","id":1440544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1440057#post1440057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the way of how V5 was done, I'm not hopeful on how Wraith &quot;5&quot; will come about. Wraith barely even has a fanbase, so even with alot people going to disagree with any potential changes, I doubt any care would be considered. I'm just waiting to see how they're going to do Werewolf &quot;5&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be the way how things are going. Between the VR game coming out and with absolutely nothing on a Mage5 (I don't count that text adventure from a few years back) or a Changeling5, and (for me at least) an off the record talk with a freelancer who said that PDX wants to do Wraith next after Werewolf, seems like it.<br /> <br /> My concern is more &quot;...do they have a plan to address Shadowguiding?&quot; I assume they have one, and to not just throw it out, since the VR game is confirmed to have the Shadow be present.<br /> <br /> Otherwise...yeah. Weird decision that it's Wraith being pushed up. It's one of my favorite WoD gamelines but...I dunno about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T09:20:13-07:00","id":1440609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My concern is more &quot;...do they have a plan to address Shadowguiding?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The best way (in my opinion of course) to handle Shadowguiding is to simply have the player roleplay their own Shadow along with their own Wraith. I know the core with how the Shadow is supposed to be done is unpredictability, but I find that since the Shadow is so integral to the player's Wraith and is often so personal, only the player would know how to roleplay them best. It also helps with pacing and allows the players more agency; even if that agency is self-sabotage via the Shadow for the interest sake of cool drama. <br /> <br /> It also makes sense for the players to have full control of their Shadow anyway, since base non-homebrew rules stipulate that the player remains control of their Wraith when the other player Shadowguiding succeeds a Catharsis roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T10:46:12-07:00","id":1440616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1440609#post1440609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The best way (in my opinion of course) to handle Shadowguiding is to simply have the player roleplay their own Shadow along with their own Wraith. I know the core with how the Shadow is supposed to be done is unpredictability, but I find that since the Shadow is so integral to the player's Wraith and is often so personal, only the player would know how to roleplay them best. It also helps with pacing and allows the players more agency; even if that agency is self-sabotage via the Shadow for the interest sake of cool drama. <br /> <br /> It also makes sense for the players to have full control of their Shadow anyway, since base non-homebrew rules stipulate that the player remains control of their Wraith when the other player Shadowguiding succeeds a Catharsis roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, for the sole reason that that doesn\u2019t really solve the logistical issues of Shadowguiding. <br /> <br /> The above approach still has each player controlling two characters at once, with the only difference being a switch in who\u2019s the Shadowguide, which is going to be a headache for players to juggle. <br /> <br /> Me personally, in terms of what I feel is the more likely course, is to just abstract the Shadow out to the point of being discrete dice rolls and nothing else, with any RP being optional at best. <br /> <br /> I admit I don\u2019t really like that option, but honestly there isn\u2019t really a good solution to fixing Shadowguiding without throwing it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 03-20-2021, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T11:49:00-07:00","id":1440739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1440057#post1440057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the way of how V5 was done, I'm not hopeful on how Wraith &quot;5&quot; will come about. Wraith barely even has a fanbase, so even with alot people going to disagree with any potential changes, I doubt any care would be considered. I'm just waiting to see how they're going to do Werewolf &quot;5&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not having a self-identified fanbase is usually a strength when it comes to new editions. It means the people who will pick it up are more likely to have an open mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T11:52:50-07:00","id":1440740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1440609#post1440609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The best way (in my opinion of course) to handle Shadowguiding is to simply have the player roleplay their own Shadow along with their own Wraith. I know the core with how the Shadow is supposed to be done is unpredictability, but I find that since the Shadow is so integral to the player's Wraith and is often so personal, only the player would know how to roleplay them best. It also helps with pacing and allows the players more agency; even if that agency is self-sabotage via the Shadow for the interest sake of cool drama.<br /> <br /> It also makes sense for the players to have full control of their Shadow anyway, since base non-homebrew rules stipulate that the player remains control of their Wraith when the other player Shadowguiding succeeds a Catharsis roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>That takes away from the dynamic of the game. The player does have a say in the design of their own Shadow, but having another player of ST play the Shadow brings an antagonism to the game that would be difficult to do if a player plays their own Shadow. Shadowplay is how players end up experiencing personal horror in the game, with the feeling that they are in conflict with their dark psyche which they cannot control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-31T19:06:08-07:00","id":1442220,"title":"","content":"Since I'm not a designer working officially at Wraith (who knows if one day maybe), I'm thinking more of a homebrewy way for the moment. And at my mind I see a Wraith setting that since the mess at the Underworld, has the wraiths more closely playing with the Shadowlands, and less on the Tempest and Kingdoms. Maybe the Labyrinth has more ways into it, for the hell of wraiths, like it has grown bigger and more rooted.<br /> There should be more factions gameplay, especially with the Hierarchy shooked up, like a vanilla Anarch wraiths experience. The wraiths should feel more than ever like the Shadow is the bastard that keeps them &quot;alive&quot; (in a world falling apart) at the same time that is plotting against it. I think a hunger dice thing isn't necessary, but a Dark Compulsion would be interesting, and there can always be extra shadow dice being offered (especially after the wraith has rolled). <br /> <br /> I'm really not sure about how Morality/Integrity or even Harrowings could work, but I bet anything post-V5/W20 would be fun. Arcanoi could have alt. powers per level I think, it always gives that mysterious vibe to have something like that. <br /> <br /> You could say that since the Maelstrom there would not only be more 'things' from deep within the Underworld appearing more and more on the surface, like an ecology that was disturbed by the actions of men. With that, there should be more necromancers, hunters and the alike, beside the specters and plasmic monstrosities, giving the Wraith chronicles even more options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T06:24:14-07:00","id":1442248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1442220#post1442220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I'm not a designer working officially at Wraith (who knows if one day maybe), I'm thinking more of a homebrewy way for the moment. And at my mind I see a Wraith setting that since the mess at the Underworld, has the wraiths more closely playing with the Shadowlands, and less on the Tempest and Kingdoms. Maybe the Labyrinth has more ways into it, for the hell of wraiths, like it has grown bigger and more rooted.<br /> There should be more factions gameplay, especially with the Hierarchy shooked up, like a vanilla Anarch wraiths experience. The wraiths should feel more than ever like the Shadow is the bastard that keeps them &quot;alive&quot; (in a world falling apart) at the same time that is plotting against it. I think a hunger dice thing isn't necessary, but a Dark Compulsion would be interesting, and there can always be extra shadow dice being offered (especially after the wraith has rolled).<br /> <br /> I'm really not sure about how Morality/Integrity or even Harrowings could work, but I bet anything post-V5/W20 would be fun. Arcanoi could have alt. powers per level I think, it always gives that mysterious vibe to have something like that.<br /> <br /> You could say that since the Maelstrom there would not only be more 'things' from deep within the Underworld appearing more and more on the surface, like an ecology that was disturbed by the actions of men. With that, there should be more necromancers, hunters and the alike, beside the specters and plasmic monstrosities, giving the Wraith chronicles even more options.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the Shadow as the bastard that keeps you going is a good dynamic that keeps the shadow interesting. I don't know that Wraith needs an integrity system beyond Passions, though.<br /> <br /> Regarding the more Shadowlands focus gameplay:<br /> <br /> As a homebrew this works great. There was actually a fan project in the early 00s that mapped out Wraith set during the 6th Great Maelstrom. It was centered around isolated Necropoli completely cut off from Stygia weathering the stormwinds and spectres. It was quite good and would work well as a variant setting for Wraith.<br /> <br /> Orpheus too pictured a Wraith with a massive metaphysical shakeup and no Stygia and it was also good. It could get away with that because it was a different gameline with a different focus. (On a technical level, Orpheus was probably skinlands focused and the shadowlands weren't even accessible for much of it, but that's not really important here).<br /> <br /> I'd hope that the Tempest and the Labyrinth are not cut out or restricted in any 'official' capacity, though. Though there are things that could temporarily make them inaccessible they shouldn't be gone forever. Styiga, the Tempest, and all those other locations say a lot about Wraithly existence and they shouldn't be removed unless they are replaced with something that says even more.<br /> <br /> Shaking things up, though, is a good plan. As you say, it gives even more options.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T09:54:11-07:00","id":1446619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1442248#post1442248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Styiga, the Tempest, and all those other locations say a lot about Wraithly existence and they shouldn't be removed unless they are replaced with something that says even more.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my objection to so many destruction of a setting, of turning an established setting into a post Apoco setting. These revisions take the interesting aspects of the setting, those portions which have something interesting to say about the setting and game, and replace them with nothing. The game and setting are not made more interesting, but less interesting. There is less to provide story hooks, less to be compelling for the players and the characters.<br /> <br /> Getting rid of Styiga, the Tempest, and other core aspects of Wraith can work if they are replaced with something at least as interesting and as useful. The revisions Orphus imposed on the setting replaced Styiga, the Tempest, and other core aspects with gravel and ashes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T16:00:38-07:00","id":1446678,"title":"","content":"To be fair, Orpheus was a very Skinland-centric game as opposed to WtO which was focused on the Underworld. It wasn't until the last or second last book that we actually got to see the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Which is understandable given the nature of the game compared to it's predecessor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T17:53:18-07:00","id":1446704,"title":"","content":"That's why I feel Orpheus never resonated with me. It tried to be too much like a Mage/Technocrat style game and little to do with being an atleast tenuous spirit-successor to Wraith. It also went down avenues with the lore and metaphysics of the Low Umbra I didn't like either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T05:11:08-07:00","id":1447179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1446704#post1446704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I feel Orpheus never resonated with me. It tried to be too much like a Mage/Technocrat style game and little to do with being an atleast tenuous spirit-successor to Wraith. It also went down avenues with the lore and metaphysics of the Low Umbra I didn't like either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Orpheus was always going to be a roll of the dice. I think if I had approached Orpheus as a replacement for Wraith, I would have been crushingly disappointed. <br /> <br /> For me the dedication to the new metaphysics and the new theme made Orpheus a great setting. It followed its themes to the hilt and I appreciate that. It very clearly doesn't work with the rest of the WoD, though, especially Wraith. I like it as its own thing, but I have no interest in projectors dealing with established Necropoli and Stygian politics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T13:18:50-07:00","id":1447253,"title":"","content":"I know it came roughly 5 years before the Time of Judgment that ended the rest of the lines, but I tend to treat End of Empire the same way that I treat Gehenna, Apocalypse, and Ascension: <i>something</i> happened, but it wasn't the setting-ending cosmic event that those other end-of-the-line books portrayed: the setting weathered the storm \u2014 figuratively, in terms of the other lines; literally, in the case of Wraith. <br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> like the idea of Orpheus' projectors interacting with wraith society; but my own preference is to handle it more or less as a supplement for something akin to Ghost Hunters: a separate product that's designed to tackle death and the afterlife from the perspective of the living. In keeping with Wr20, I might go so far as to say that Orpheus is to Wraith as the Enchanted are to Changeling: they're mortals who partake in the world of the dead (to the point that they have some access to the Arcanoi) but are not dead. I'd ditch the end of the world plot that the original version of Orpheus had, though; the notion that the Afterlife has been wiped clean by the Maelstrom would go away. Though I'd keep the Storm itself, and just say that it wasn't quite as catastrophic as Orpheus portrays. <br /> <br /> Heck, Ends of Empire ended with the notion that the worst of it was over, and that while it would take some time, the world of the dead would recover. It was only in other gamelines (Hunter, then Orpheus) that the catastrophic nature of it got dialed up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-22-2022, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T08:22:38-07:00","id":1447713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1270742-wraith-5?p=1447253#post1447253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>do</i> like the idea of Orpheus' projectors interacting with wraith society; but my own preference is to handle it more or less as a supplement for something akin to Ghost Hunters: a separate product That's designed to tackle death and the afterlife from the perspective of the living. In keeping with Wr20, I might go so far as to say that Orpheus is to Wraith as the Enchanted are to Changeling: they're mortals who partake in the world of the dead (to the point that they have some access to the Arcanoi) but are not dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a really good way of describing what projectors would be in a regular Wraith game and why I don't find the concept any more than an idle curiosity. I love both games' take on the ghost story, but they do not play well together. Bringing projectors into Wraith requires stripping out much of what made the characters unique in Orpheus. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-22T01:40:03-07:00","id":1479283,"title":"","content":"I'm currently trying to get into Wraith seriously once more (I failed at it some years ago after collecting some books).<br /> <br /> I'll probably be in a minority, because I'm not emotionally invested on the existing game as much as I am with Vampire and Werewolf but I'm personally hoping for a Wraith 5, because I dig the streamlined rules of V5.<br /> <br /> And while the Hunger mechanic wasn't thorughly well thought as it should have been, I personally think it's a cool idea (might need some work). Used it as Madness dice in a Cthulhu game and it was fun<br /> <br /> At the same time I don't dig the sometimes too extreme &quot;pruning&quot; of the setting that V5 went through. While with time I digested some of the changes and I'm able to appreciate the coolness of some decisions, there are others that I still wish they'll be retconned as never happened in V6<br /> Especially I don't appreciate the sudden and forceful removal of the main oppressors (the elders)<br /> <br /> The more I'm reading of Wraith in the last days, the more stuff I find that is very imaginative, creative, horror, fascinating, cool. I'm having a real blast<br /> <br /> So I'm hoping for a Wraith 5 for some neat and easy-to-use mechanics, but also I'm hoping they'll limit themselves to shake up the setting up a bit (rebuilding from 6th GM sounds good) without &quot;pruning&quot; the setting of its weird, cool, and unique stuff<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}